[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965469333","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116797#issuecomment-3965469333","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116797","id":3965469333,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sXEKV","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T09:54:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T09:54:35Z","body":"This issue is documented [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#flow-control), this is probably not something we can \"fix\":\n> Keep in mind that in modern GPUs, an infinite loop can exist and can freeze your application (including editor). Godot can't protect you from this, so be careful not to make this mistake!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965469333/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965595199","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116797#issuecomment-3965595199","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116797","id":3965595199,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sXi4_","user":{"login":"carllacan","id":2113496,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTM0OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2113496?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan","html_url":"https://github.com/carllacan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T10:14:40Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T10:14:40Z","body":"> This issue is documented [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#flow-control), this is probably not something we can \"fix\":\n> \n> > Keep in mind that in modern GPUs, an infinite loop can exist and can freeze your application (including editor). Godot can't protect you from this, so be careful not to make this mistake!\n\nThat seems to be taking about infinite loops, so I don't think this is the same. Unless your suggestion is that the unassigned loop variable is making the loop run forever?\n\nI don't think that's the case, since an empty `for` statement with an uninitialized loop variable does not cause this issue. It could be that an empty loop compiles to nothing and it's effectively not an infinite loop, but I think even with an empty body the instructions that increase the loop variable should run and cause an infinite loop. I'm leaning more towards the unassigned variable pointing to garbage and causing havok.\n\nBut let's suppose it is an infinite loop. While I wouldn't expect the shader language to look for infinite loops (which would involve analyzing the code in the loop's body) I think this particular case could still be prevented by un-allowing unassigned variables in the `for` statement, if it's possible to do so. The only problems I can (naively) see would be retro-compatibility, but I don't see why anyone would purposely leave the loop variable unassigned.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965595199/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965609446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116797#issuecomment-3965609446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116797","id":3965609446,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sXmXm","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T10:17:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T10:27:11Z","body":"What I mean is that the GPU runs complex code and that this is a rendering hardware side issue rather than the engine, we can add some potential safeguards but it's not possible to protect from everything if the hardware doesn't allow it\n\nAlso unable to check the code right now but it might be because of memory access unrelated to the loop, like a negative index into an array (see [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#local-arrays) and [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#data-types))","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965609446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965709863","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116797#issuecomment-3965709863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116797","id":3965709863,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sX-4n","user":{"login":"carllacan","id":2113496,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTM0OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2113496?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan","html_url":"https://github.com/carllacan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carllacan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T10:34:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T10:35:28Z","body":"Yeah, no, I understand that shaders are complex and it's hard to prevent everything that might make them crash, I'm just saying that disallowing the use of unassigned variables would prevent _some_ of those crashes and that it seems like it would not be a huge undertaking to do so (though as I say I could be very wrong). So the cost-benefit seems to be in favor of it, at least to my untrained eye.\n\n> Also unable to check the code right now but it might be because of memory access unrelated to the loop, like a negative index into an array (see [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#local-arrays) and [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#data-types))\n\nYeah, that was my initial suspicion as well.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965709863/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965733793","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116797#issuecomment-3965733793","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116797","id":3965733793,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sYEuh","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T10:39:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T10:39:22Z","body":"It might be possible to leverage the shader translator and compiler for glsl, we do some optimizations now with that it might be possible to enable static checks there, at least for trivial cases ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965733793/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967604026","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116797#issuecomment-3967604026","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116797","id":3967604026,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sfNU6","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T16:09:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T16:09:35Z","body":"I think there were an issue recently about that Godot will eagerly compile shader code while you are not finished writing it and will crash video driver if you've written an infinite loop. Couldn't find that issue but found this one https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/42311.\nThere are also topics online where people write about this issue. It seems that the only \"fix\" for this problem is to disable shader cache in the project settings (https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/1cmswav/how_to_stop_auto_shader_compilation_driver_crash/).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967604026/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]